  "boundaries": {
    "allocation": "All marginal allocations are analyst priors summing to one, not audited fractions. Remaining 80% of central gift retained in denominator and unquantified. Offers include branch costs; separately allocated corporate costs not charged again.",
    "od": "Unique people counted alive at intervention start, not gift date: compare recurrent-event survival curves through finite horizon. Expected service-start caseload already conditions on survival to care. Baseline rescue and treatment already occur. Active support ends then recurrent hazard returns to baseline; deaths delayed, not permanently prevented. No separate credit for doses/reversals, MOUD/HCV or HIV endpoints.",
    "housing": "One adult-equivalent per household. .112 external observational stable-at-exit risk difference × .5 transfer gives .056 local stable-day probability difference for one year by explicit prior. Utility gap .1 is morbidity-only analyst prior; no VA .144/.072 QALY transfer, perfect-health assumption, mortality effect or child multiplier. Housing baseline .8 is local illustrative prior, not VA .821 observation.",
    "overlap": "Housing benefits limited to adults outside OD health cohort by .9 disjoint prior. All housing costs and shared harms remain for excluded people. Nonquantified other programs receive no stacked health credit.",
    "timing": "Both cohorts are expected people alive at intervention start; service-start caseload already conditions on pre-service survival, so delay only discounts health and no pre-service survival multiplier is added. Housing duration capped at two years computationally; central one year, constant probability difference is a persistence prior. Common housing mortality weights both arms equally after care begins. OD horizon 15 years central, active1 year. Discount3%, explicit service delays. All harms are gift-date PV QALY losses, distinct from signed clinical worsening.",
    "resources": "Associated funding envelope = full gift plus nominal offered service outside resource priors. Modeled resource cost removes donor-funded rent-transfer prior once. External resources are non-transfer staff/supplies/partner real costs not paid by donor; incurred per nominal offer, including replaced/deduplicated activity. No induced savings credited. Not a validated societal ledger: other transfers, housing service opportunity costs, in-kind and public displacement remain uncertain.",
    "geography": "Future person-health location shares, not clinic address: OD Bay .99 SF .95; housing Bay .98 SF .95; harm Bay .98 SF .95. All unverified, independently nested; US total excludes unmodeled overseas effects.",
    "funding_room": "Unknown not zero. Government, SF ERAP, Season of Sharing, problem-solving services, SFAF subcontract and existing donor-funded stock belong in baseline. Proposed public contract not guaranteed new money. No current unfunded queue or executable gift tranche."
  },
